---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '10 August 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — WP Base"
  description="How WP Base collects, uses and protects your personal information. Written in plain English rather than legal boilerplate."
>
  <section class="legal-header-section">
    <div class="legal-reading">
      <span class="section-label">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="legal-headline">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <p class="legal-lead">
        This policy explains what personal information WP Base collects, why it is
        collected, and what you can do about it. It covers this website, enquiry
        forms, email correspondence and any paid care plans.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-body-section">
    <div class="legal-reading">
      <h2>Who is responsible for your information</h2>
      <p>
        WP Base is a WordPress maintenance and web design business run by Chris
        Kernaghan, based in Newtownabbey, Northern Ireland. WP Base is the data
        controller for the information described here.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have a question about this policy or about your information, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@wpbase.co.uk">hello@wpbase.co.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What information is collected</h2>
      <p>
        The amount of information collected depends on how you interact with WP Base.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiries and audit requests.</strong> When you complete a form on
          this site, you provide your name, email address, and whatever details you
          choose to include about your website or business. Some forms also ask for a
          phone number or website URL.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email correspondence.</strong> If you email directly, that message
          and your email address are held in the WP Base mailbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Care plan customers.</strong> If you subscribe to a plan, billing
          details are collected and processed by Stripe. WP Base does not see or store
          your full card number. Records of invoices and subscriptions are kept for
          accounting purposes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client site access.</strong> Where WP Base maintains your website,
          this involves access to hosting accounts, WordPress administration and
          related credentials. That access is used only for the work you have asked
          for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics.</strong> With your consent, analytics and
          advertising cookies record pages viewed, approximate location, device and
          browser type, and how you arrived at the site.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why it is collected, and the lawful basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>To respond to your enquiry.</strong> Lawful basis: legitimate
          interests, in that you have contacted a business expecting a reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To deliver services you have paid for.</strong> Lawful basis:
          performance of a contract.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To keep accounting and tax records.</strong> Lawful basis: legal
          obligation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To measure how the website and any advertising performs.</strong>
          Lawful basis: consent, given through the cookie banner and withdrawable at
          any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To send occasional updates, where you have asked for them.</strong>
          Lawful basis: consent. Every message includes an unsubscribe link.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who else handles your information</h2>
      <p>
        WP Base does not sell your information and does not share it for anyone else's
        marketing. A small number of service providers process data on WP Base's behalf
        in order to run the business.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> for website hosting and security.</li>
        <li><strong>Fillout</strong> for enquiry and audit request forms.</li>
        <li><strong>Zoho Mail</strong> for email.</li>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong> for payments and subscription billing.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager</strong> for website
          measurement, where you have consented.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>LinkedIn</strong> for advertising and conversion measurement, where
          you have consented.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of these providers are based outside the UK. Where that is the case,
        transfers are covered by the UK International Data Transfer Agreement, the UK
        Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, or an adequacy decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Information may also be disclosed where there is a legal requirement to do so.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets cookies that are necessary for it to work, and these do not
        require your consent. Analytics and advertising cookies are only set after you
        agree through the cookie banner. You can change or withdraw that choice at any
        time using the cookie settings link in the footer, and you can block or delete
        cookies in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiries that do not become work:</strong> up to two years, then
          deleted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client records and correspondence:</strong> for the length of the
          working relationship and six years afterwards.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Invoices and financial records:</strong> six years, as required by
          HMRC.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics data:</strong> in line with the retention period set in
          Google Analytics, currently 14 months.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask WP Base to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>confirm what information is held about you, and give you a copy;</li>
        <li>correct anything that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
        <li>delete your information, where there is no reason to keep it;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to how it is used;</li>
        <li>transfer it to another provider in a portable format;</li>
        <li>stop sending you marketing, at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:hello@wpbase.co.uk">hello@wpbase.co.uk</a> and you will
        get a response within one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how your information has been handled, you can complain
        to the Information Commissioner's Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, by phone on 0303
        123 1113, or by post to Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9
        5AF.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts are protected with strong unique passwords and two-factor
        authentication where it is available. Client credentials are stored in a
        password manager rather than in email or plain text files. No system is
        completely secure, but reasonable technical and organisational measures are in
        place to protect what is held.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated as the business or its tools change. The date at the
        top shows when it was last revised.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-header-section {
    padding: 7rem 1.5rem 2rem;
  }
  .legal-body-section {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 5rem;
  }
  .legal-reading {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .legal-headline {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    font-family: 'Epilogue', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    opacity: 0.65;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal-lead {
    font-family: 'Epilogue', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    opacity: 0.9;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal-reading h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal-reading p,
  .legal-reading li {
    font-family: 'Epilogue', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .legal-reading p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-reading ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-reading li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .legal-reading a {
    color: var(--midnight);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .legal-header-section {
      padding-top: 5.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
